# WebWeaver Nexus MCP server — local development environment.
#
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored). Both variables are read ONLY in server.ts, on
# the server side: src/mcp-app.ts is bundled into a ~435 KB HTML string served
# to every user, so the secret must never be imported into it. After building,
# `grep -c 'CONTACT_FORM_SHARED_SECRET' generated/mcp-app-html.ts` must be 0.
#
# `npm run serve` loads this file from the working directory. The stdio entry
# point (`npm run serve:stdio`, and Claude Desktop) runs with cwd=/ and cannot
# find it — put an `env` block in claude_desktop_config.json instead.

# Where submit_contact_form POSTs. No trailing slash (one is stripped anyway).
#
# Keep this pointed at a LOCAL landing page while developing. Against
# production, every test submission writes a real row to the production
# Supabase table and sends two real emails. Vercel *preview* deployments of
# this server do point at production — use them sparingly, and clean up the
# rows afterwards (they carry source='mcp').
CONTACT_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Must match CONTACT_FORM_SHARED_SECRET in the landing page's .env.local.
# A mismatch surfaces as a 401 from the contact API, which looks like a form
# bug and is not — check these two values agree before debugging anything else.
CONTACT_FORM_SHARED_SECRET=local-dev-secret
